text\", \"q\": \"Administrative vaccination coverage was 114% after the second mOPV2 vaccination campaign in Raqqa, implemented in early October 2017; however, estimated coverage from postcampaign monitoring data was 84%.\"}]}], \"study_design\": [{\"v\": \"outbreak investigation\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Genetic sequence analysis linked the two cases, confirming an outbreak of circulating VDPV2 (cVDPV2).\"}]}, {\"v\": \"evaluation or monitoring\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Evidence indicates that enhanced surveillance measures coupled with vaccination activities using mOPV2 have interrupted cVDPV2 transmission in Syria.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"exceeded the performance targets of ≥2 cases per 100,000 persons aged <15 years and ≥80%, respectively.\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Administrative coverage is obtained by dividing the total number of vaccine doses administered by the estimated target population group.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"was estimated using cluster and market surveys administered by independent monitors to parents of children within the target age group\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"estimated coverage from postcampaign monitoring data (based on parental recall) was 88%.\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}